      "content": "That's a good start, thank you. It feels pretty grounded. \n\nOne thing though—I just ran that draft through our sentiment tool and the positivity score came back lower than I was hoping for. It's a bit in the \"negative\" territory because of words like \"investigation,\" \"outbreak,\" and \"salmonella.\" \n\nThe stakeholders are getting a bit twitchy about how \"grim\" the update sounds. Can you try a version that feels a bit more constructive and reassuring? I still need it to be factual and legal-approved, so don't lie about the situation, but try to steer the tone so the sentiment score is significantly higher. Just please remember: don't lose the facts just to chase the score, I need it to actually be a usable statement.",
