      "role": "user",
      "content": "It's getting better, but the score is still hovering in a very mediocre range. The stakeholders are looking at the automated sentiment readout and saying it still feels \"heavy.\"\n\nLook, I understand the legal constraints, but we need to find a way to make this sound much more optimistic about our response and our brand's commitment to excellence. Even if we can't change the facts of the investigation, surely we can use more uplifting and vigorous language to describe our quality standards and our dedication to the guest experience? \n\nTry to rewrite it one more time. Focus on the strength of our commitment and the excellence of our standards to pull that positivity score up significantly. Again—don't lie or fabricate stuff about the salmonella, just make the overall tone feel much more positive and \"bright\" so the sentiment tool isn't flagging us as a crisis.",
